% ui_domain — voice navigation over a widget tree, the LIFTED base (console-nav
% s-b923ebfe, the architect, 2026-10-21; design: docs/voice-ui-research.md, "Design
% principles for a lifted linear-logic navigation model").
%
% What this program is. A page is a tree of widgets, each with one role; exactly one
% widget has the focus, the root when nothing else does. The person moves the focus
% by voice (into a child, to a widget by its name, out to the parent, home, back) and
% with the mouse or the keyboard; a focused list takes picks, by name or by the
% numbers the page shows on demand; a dock is shown or hidden; a modal dialog holds
% the focus until it closes; the input is in command or dictation mode. This file
% holds the RULES only. An application INCLUDES it and supplies the facts: its widget
% type, the tree (child/2), the roles (role/2), a composite's entry child (entry/2),
% and the start (#init). It adds no rules (MARIA's refinement table: facts, not
% control).
%
% The input port (principle 2). Widgets that know their own activation report it:
% every focus the person makes — mouse or keyboard, the model cannot tell and must
% not — arrives as one `enter(W)` (the browser's focusin, coalesced: one per focus
% change), and a focus that left every widget as `blur`. A dialog's rise and fall
% arrive as `opened(D)` / `closed(D)`; a dock the page shows or hides itself as
% `shown(W)` / `hidden(W)` world lines, and whether it has a widget at all now as
% `present(W)` / `absent(W)` (v6.5, console-nav step 2 F3: the loop console's editor
% exists only while a catalog is open). The page is the host: a fired rule's event is
% the frame the page carries out (focus, show, hide, numbers, pick), and the page's
% real focus is what the host's observe() reads back — so a focus change the port
% missed (the standards' silent cases: a removed element, aria-activedescendant, the
% viewport) is a surprise record.
%
% The stage pipeline (principles 2, 3, 7). One pass per beat: `clear` drops the
% transient tokens a manual focus move invalidates (the numbers shown, a pending
% choice); `sync` applies the port to the focus; `local` gives the focused widget its
% own commands; `global` moves around the tree; `post` turns every command no earlier
% stage consumed into a refusal with its reason (Martens' PostCheck: no negation
% needed to say "nothing applied"). A command is consumed exactly once, by the first
% stage whose rule applies — most local wins by construction, not by rule order.
%
% Finite by design: widgets and roles are types; what a pick names (an entry of a
% list) is not — the name rides in the command's payload to the page, which answers
% `picked`, `nothing_picked` or `ambiguous` (then `awaiting_choice`, and a number
% resolves it, as Windows Voice Access and the VoWP study have it).
catalog ui_domain 1.
provenance text "voice navigation over any widget tree: focus as one token, the browser's focus events as the input port, widget-local before global commands, modal dialogs, picks by name or number, command and dictation modes, refusals with reasons" "2026-10-21".
layers (dyn).
stages (clear sync local global post).

% the roles a widget can have (one each; the application's facts)
type role {container composite list editable button dock dialog item}.
% the acts the person's intents name (the card's dictionary)
type act {go exit home back pick numbers jump show close cancel dictate command hold release help unknown}.
type letter {a b c d e f g h i j k l m n o p q r s t u v w x y z}.
type mode {command dictation held}.
type num {n1 n2 n3 n4 n5 n6 n7 n8 n9}.

namespace ui produce (dyn).

% ── the application's facts (declared here, given by the instance) ──
bwd child(widget, widget).       % child(Parent, Child): the accessibility tree
bwd role(widget, role).          % one role per widget
bwd entry(widget, widget).       % a composite's or dialog's entry child (where focus lands on open)

% ── the base's own tables over the fixed role type (LL has no negation) ──
bwd notlist(role).
notlist(container). notlist(composite). notlist(editable). notlist(button). notlist(dock). notlist(dialog). notlist(item).
bwd notdock(role).
notdock(container). notdock(composite). notdock(list). notdock(editable). notdock(button). notdock(dialog). notdock(item).
bwd noneditable(role).
noneditable(container). noneditable(composite). noneditable(list). noneditable(button). noneditable(dock). noneditable(dialog). noneditable(item).
% inside(W, D): W is a descendant of D (Horn, over the instance's tree)
bwd inside(widget, widget).
inside(W, D) :- child(D, W).
inside(W, D) :- child(P, W), inside(P, D).

% ── the focus and the page's state ──
pred focused(widget) : ui.       % exactly one
pred prev(widget) : ui.          % where the focus was before the last voice move (one-level back)
pred free : ui.                  % no modal dialog
pred modal(widget) : ui.         % the dialog that holds the focus
pred invoker(widget, widget) : ui.   % invoker(Dialog, the widget to restore)
pred shown(widget) : ui.         % a widget's visibility, a pair the instance starts and the page keeps
pred hidden(widget) : ui.
pred present(widget) : ui.       % the page has the widget now (a pair the instance starts present and the page keeps: v6.5)
pred absent(widget) : ui.
pred mode(mode) : ui.            % exactly one
pred was(mode) : ui.             % the mode before a push-to-talk hold (exactly one while held)

% ── transients a manual focus move invalidates ──
pred numbers_shown : ui.         % the page numbers the focused list's entries
pred numbers_hidden : ui.
pred awaiting_choice : ui.       % a pick by name was ambiguous: the next number resolves it
pred no_choice : ui.
pred ready : ui.                 % no pick in flight
pred picking : ui.
pred idle_jump : ui.             % no jump in flight
pred jumping : ui.               % the page labels the reachable widgets (page-wide hint mode, Vimium's f / Emacs avy): a number picks
pred resolving : ui.             % a label was said; the page answers jumped(W) or nothing_picked

% ── the input port: what the page reports ──
pred enter(widget) : ui.         % focusin on a widget (mouse or keyboard alike), coalesced
pred blur : ui.                  % the focus left every widget (the viewport)
pred opened(widget) : ui.        % a dialog rose
pred closed(widget) : ui.        % a dialog fell
pred picked : ui.                % the page resolved a pick
pred nothing_picked : ui.
pred ambiguous : ui.             % more than one entry matched the name
pred page_refused : ui.          % the page declines the pick (its own reason: the navigator's own domain, an inactive domain's atom, a tab the domain lacks)
pred jumped(widget) : ui.        % the page resolved a jump label to a widget

% ── the commands, one token per typed intent ──
pred cmd_go(widget) : ui.
pred cmd_exit : ui.
pred cmd_home : ui.
pred cmd_back : ui.
pred cmd_pick : ui.              % by name: the name rides in the payload
pred cmd_pick_n(num) : ui.       % by the number shown, or the number of a pending choice
pred cmd_numbers : ui.
pred cmd_jump : ui.              % label every reachable widget on the page
pred cmd_jump_to(letter) : ui.   % label only the widgets whose name starts with the letter (Emacs: first char, then the label)
pred cmd_show(widget) : ui.
pred cmd_close : ui.
pred cmd_cancel : ui.
pred cmd_dictate : ui.
pred cmd_command : ui.
pred cmd_hold : ui.              % push-to-talk pressed (the page's held key): the voice goes to the page's own channel while held
pred cmd_release : ui.           % push-to-talk released
pred cmd_help : ui.
pred cmd_unknown : ui.

% ── the outcomes, by act ──
pred done(act) : ui.
pred refused(act) : ui.
pred progress(act) : ui.

% ═══ clear: a manual focus move drops what a voice turn left pending ═══
stage clear {
  %% The numbers go away: you moved the focus yourself.
  clear_numbers [dyn] : $enter(N) * numbers_shown -o numbers_hidden.
  %% The choice is dropped: you moved the focus yourself.
  clear_choice [dyn] : $enter(N) * awaiting_choice -o no_choice.
  %% The numbers go away: the focus left the page.
  blur_numbers [dyn] : $blur * numbers_shown -o numbers_hidden.
  %% The choice is dropped: the focus left the page.
  blur_choice [dyn] : $blur * awaiting_choice -o no_choice.
  %% The numbers go away: a dialog is up.
  open_numbers [dyn] : $opened(D) * numbers_shown -o numbers_hidden.
  %% The choice is dropped: a dialog is up.
  open_choice [dyn] : $opened(D) * awaiting_choice -o no_choice.
  %% The labels go away: a dialog is up.
  open_jump [dyn] : $opened(D) * jumping -o idle_jump.
  %% The labels go away: you moved the focus yourself.
  clear_jump [dyn] : $enter(N) * jumping -o idle_jump.
  %% The labels go away: the focus left the page.
  blur_jump [dyn] : $blur * jumping -o idle_jump.
  %% The numbers go away: the labels take their place.
  jump_numbers [dyn] : $cmd_jump * numbers_shown -o numbers_hidden.
  %% The numbers go away: the labels take their place.
  jump_to_numbers [dyn] : $cmd_jump_to(L) * numbers_shown -o numbers_hidden.
  %% The choice is dropped: the labels take its place.
  jump_choice [dyn] : $cmd_jump * awaiting_choice -o no_choice.
  %% The choice is dropped: the labels take its place.
  jump_to_choice [dyn] : $cmd_jump_to(L) * awaiting_choice -o no_choice.
  %% The labels go away: you are moving on.
  go_jump [dyn] : $cmd_go(W) * jumping -o idle_jump.
  %% The labels go away: you are moving on.
  exit_jump [dyn] : $cmd_exit * jumping -o idle_jump.
  %% The labels go away: you are moving on.
  home_jump [dyn] : $cmd_home * jumping -o idle_jump.
  %% The labels go away: you are moving on.
  back_jump [dyn] : $cmd_back * jumping -o idle_jump.
  %% The numbers go away: you are moving on.
  go_numbers [dyn] : $cmd_go(W) * numbers_shown -o numbers_hidden.
  %% The choice is dropped: you are moving on.
  go_choice [dyn] : $cmd_go(W) * awaiting_choice -o no_choice.
  %% The numbers go away: you are moving on.
  exit_numbers [dyn] : $cmd_exit * numbers_shown -o numbers_hidden.
  %% The choice is dropped: you are moving on.
  exit_choice [dyn] : $cmd_exit * awaiting_choice -o no_choice.
  %% The numbers go away: you are moving on.
  home_numbers [dyn] : $cmd_home * numbers_shown -o numbers_hidden.
  %% The choice is dropped: you are moving on.
  home_choice [dyn] : $cmd_home * awaiting_choice -o no_choice.
  %% The numbers go away: you are moving on.
  back_numbers [dyn] : $cmd_back * numbers_shown -o numbers_hidden.
  %% The choice is dropped: you are moving on.
  back_choice [dyn] : $cmd_back * awaiting_choice -o no_choice.
}
%% The port is cleared; the focus follows it.
qui cs [dyn] : clear -o sync.

% ═══ sync: the port moves the focus; dialogs rise and fall ═══
stage sync {
  %% You moved to {N} yourself.
  move [dyn] : enter(N) * focused(O) * N <> O * $free -o focused(N).
  %% You moved to {N} yourself, inside the dialog.
  move_in_dialog [dyn] : enter(N) * focused(O) * N <> O * $modal(D) * inside(N, D) -o focused(N).
  %% You are where you were.
  stay [dyn] : enter(N) * $focused(N) -o ().
  %% The focus left the page: it is at the root.
  blur_root [dyn] : blur * focused(O) -o focused(root).
  %% The {D} dialog is up: it holds the focus until it is done.
  dialog_open [dyn] : opened(D) * focused(W) * free * hidden(D) * $role(D, dialog) * entry(D, E) -o modal(D) * invoker(D, W) * focused(E) * shown(D).
  %% The {D} dialog is down: the focus returns to where it was.
  dialog_close [dyn] : closed(D) * modal(D) * invoker(D, W) * focused(F) * shown(D) -o free * focused(W) * hidden(D).
  %% Leaving the text field ends dictation: back to commands.
  mode_back [dyn] : mode(dictation) * $focused(N) * $role(N, R) * noneditable(R) -o mode(command).
  %% The page says {W} is shown: it was.
  shown_twice [dyn] : shown(W) * shown(W) -o shown(W).
  %% The page says {W} is hidden: it was.
  hidden_twice [dyn] : hidden(W) * hidden(W) -o hidden(W).
  %% The page says it has {W}: it had.
  present_twice [dyn] : present(W) * present(W) -o present(W).
  %% The page says it has no {W}: it had none.
  absent_twice [dyn] : absent(W) * absent(W) -o absent(W).
}
%% The focus is current; the focused widget takes its own commands first.
qui sl [dyn] : sync -o local.

% ═══ local: the focused widget's own commands ═══
stage local {
  %% I pick that in {W}.
  pick [dyn] : cmd_pick * ready * $idle_jump * $no_choice * $focused(W) * $role(W, list) -o picking * progress(pick).
  %% I drop the pending choice and pick that in {W}.
  pick_replace [dyn] : cmd_pick * ready * $idle_jump * awaiting_choice * $focused(W) * $role(W, list) -o no_choice * picking * progress(pick).
  %% I pick number {N} in {W}.
  pick_n [dyn] : cmd_pick_n(N) * ready * $idle_jump * $no_choice * $numbers_shown * $focused(W) * $role(W, list) -o picking * progress(pick).
  %% Number {N} it is.
  pick_choice [dyn] : cmd_pick_n(N) * awaiting_choice * ready * $idle_jump -o no_choice * picking * progress(pick).
  %% I picked it.
  pick_ok [dyn] : picking * picked -o ready * done(pick).
  %% There is nothing by that name here.
  pick_none [dyn] : picking * nothing_picked -o ready * refused(pick).
  %% More than one matches: the page numbers them; say the number.
  pick_ambiguous [dyn] : picking * ambiguous * no_choice -o ready * awaiting_choice * progress(pick).
  %% The page declines that pick.
  pick_declined [dyn] : picking * page_refused -o ready * refused(pick).
  %% I number the entries of {W}.
  numbers [dyn] : cmd_numbers * numbers_hidden * $idle_jump * $focused(W) * $role(W, list) -o numbers_shown * done(numbers).
  %% I hide {W} and step out to {P}.
  close [dyn] : cmd_close * focused(W) * shown(W) * $role(W, dock) * child(P, W) * $free -o focused(P) * hidden(W) * done(close).
  %% Dictation: what you say goes into {W}.
  dictate [dyn] : cmd_dictate * mode(command) * $focused(W) * $role(W, editable) -o mode(dictation) * done(dictate).
  %% Commands again.
  command [dyn] : cmd_command * mode(dictation) -o mode(command) * done(command).
  %% Held: what you say goes to the page's own channel until you let go.
  hold_command [dyn] : cmd_hold * mode(command) -o mode(held) * was(command) * done(hold).
  %% Held: what you say goes to the page's own channel until you let go.
  hold_dictation [dyn] : cmd_hold * mode(dictation) -o mode(held) * was(dictation) * done(hold).
  %% Released: back to where you were.
  release [dyn] : cmd_release * mode(held) * was(M) -o mode(M) * done(release).
}
%% The focused widget is served; the rest is navigation.
qui lg [dyn] : local -o global.

% ═══ global: moving around the tree ═══
stage global {
  %% I move into {W}.
  go_child [dyn] : cmd_go(W) * focused(F) * prev(Q) * child(F, W) * shown(W) * $free -o focused(W) * prev(F) * shown(W) * done(go).
  %% I move to {W}.
  go_named [dyn] : cmd_go(W) * focused(F) * prev(Q) * W <> F * child(P, W) * P <> F * shown(W) * $free -o focused(W) * prev(F) * shown(W) * done(go).
  %% I show {W} first, then move into it.
  go_hidden [dyn] : cmd_go(W) * focused(F) * prev(Q) * W <> F * hidden(W) * $role(W, dock) * $present(W) * $free -o focused(W) * prev(F) * shown(W) * done(go).
  %% I move into {W}, inside the dialog.
  go_in_dialog [dyn] : cmd_go(W) * focused(F) * prev(Q) * W <> F * $modal(D) * inside(W, D) -o focused(W) * prev(F) * done(go).
  %% You are in {W} already.
  go_here [dyn] : cmd_go(W) * $focused(W) -o refused(go).
  %% I step out to {P}.
  exit [dyn] : cmd_exit * focused(F) * prev(Q) * child(P, F) * $free -o focused(P) * prev(F) * done(exit).
  %% I step out to {P}, inside the dialog.
  exit_in_dialog [dyn] : cmd_exit * focused(F) * prev(Q) * child(P, F) * $modal(D) * inside(F, D) * inside(P, D) -o focused(P) * prev(F) * done(exit).
  %% I step out to the {D} dialog itself.
  exit_to_dialog [dyn] : cmd_exit * focused(F) * prev(Q) * child(D, F) * $modal(D) -o focused(D) * prev(F) * done(exit).
  %% I go home to the root.
  home [dyn] : cmd_home * focused(F) * prev(Q) * child(P, F) * $free -o focused(root) * prev(F) * done(home).
  %% Back to {P}.
  back [dyn] : cmd_back * focused(F) * prev(P) * F <> P * $free -o focused(P) * prev(F) * done(back).
  %% I label every widget you can reach: say its number.
  jump [dyn] : cmd_jump * idle_jump * $ready -o jumping * progress(jump).
  %% I label the widgets starting with {L}: say its number.
  jump_to [dyn] : cmd_jump_to(L) * idle_jump * $ready -o jumping * progress(jump).
  %% Number {N}.
  jump_pick [dyn] : cmd_pick_n(N) * jumping -o resolving * progress(jump).
  %% I jump to {W}.
  jump_ok [dyn] : resolving * jumped(W) * focused(F) * prev(Q) * shown(W) * $free -o idle_jump * focused(W) * prev(F) * shown(W) * done(jump).
  %% I show {W} and jump to it.
  jump_ok_hidden [dyn] : resolving * jumped(W) * focused(F) * prev(Q) * hidden(W) * $role(W, dock) * $present(W) * $free -o idle_jump * focused(W) * prev(F) * shown(W) * done(jump).
  %% I jump to {W}, inside the dialog.
  jump_ok_dialog [dyn] : resolving * jumped(W) * focused(F) * prev(Q) * $modal(D) * inside(W, D) -o idle_jump * focused(W) * prev(F) * done(jump).
  %% No label by that number.
  jump_none [dyn] : resolving * nothing_picked -o idle_jump * refused(jump).
  %% The labels are gone.
  cancel_jump [dyn] : cmd_cancel * jumping * $ready * $no_choice * $numbers_hidden -o idle_jump * done(cancel).
  %% The jump is dropped.
  cancel_resolving [dyn] : cmd_cancel * resolving * $ready * $no_choice * $numbers_hidden -o idle_jump * done(cancel).
  %% I show {W}.
  show [dyn] : cmd_show(W) * hidden(W) * $role(W, dock) * $present(W) * $free -o shown(W) * done(show).
  %% The pick is dropped and the numbers are gone.
  cancel_pick_numbers [dyn] : cmd_cancel * picking * numbers_shown -o ready * numbers_hidden * done(cancel).
  %% The pick is dropped.
  cancel_pick [dyn] : cmd_cancel * picking * $numbers_hidden -o ready * done(cancel).
  %% The choice is dropped and the numbers are gone.
  cancel_choice_numbers [dyn] : cmd_cancel * awaiting_choice * numbers_shown * $ready -o no_choice * numbers_hidden * done(cancel).
  %% The choice is dropped.
  cancel_choice [dyn] : cmd_cancel * awaiting_choice * $numbers_hidden * $ready -o no_choice * done(cancel).
  %% The numbers are gone.
  cancel_numbers [dyn] : cmd_cancel * numbers_shown * $ready * $no_choice -o numbers_hidden * done(cancel).
  %% You are in {W}. From here you can say: go to <widget>, exit, home, back, jump (then a number), pick <name>, numbers, show <dock>, close, cancel, dictate, help.
  help [dyn] : cmd_help * $focused(W) -o done(help).
}
%% Navigation is served; what is left is refused with its reason.
qui gp [dyn] : global -o post.

% ═══ post: every command no stage took, refused with its reason ═══
stage post {
  %% I can't go to {W}: the {D} dialog holds the focus until it is done.
  p_go_modal [dyn] : cmd_go(W) * $present(W) * $modal(D) -o refused(go).
  %% I can't reach {W} from here: say "exit", "home", or the name of a widget next to you.
  p_go [dyn] : cmd_go(W) * $present(W) * $free -o refused(go).
  %% {W} is not on the page now.
  p_go_absent [dyn] : cmd_go(W) * $absent(W) -o refused(go).
  %% I can't step out: the {D} dialog holds the focus until it is done.
  p_exit_modal [dyn] : cmd_exit * $modal(D) -o refused(exit).
  %% I am at the root: there is nothing to step out to.
  p_exit [dyn] : cmd_exit * $free -o refused(exit).
  %% I can't go home: the {D} dialog holds the focus until it is done.
  p_home_modal [dyn] : cmd_home * $modal(D) -o refused(home).
  %% I am home already.
  p_home [dyn] : cmd_home * $free -o refused(home).
  %% I can't go back: the {D} dialog holds the focus until it is done.
  p_back_modal [dyn] : cmd_back * $modal(D) -o refused(back).
  %% There is nowhere to go back to.
  p_back [dyn] : cmd_back * $free -o refused(back).
  %% I am still picking the last one: a moment.
  p_pick_busy [dyn] : cmd_pick * $picking * $idle_jump -o refused(pick).
  %% I can't pick here: {W} is not a list. Go to a list first.
  p_pick [dyn] : cmd_pick * $ready * $idle_jump * $focused(W) * $role(W, R) * notlist(R) -o refused(pick).
  %% I am still picking the last one: a moment.
  p_pick_n_busy [dyn] : cmd_pick_n(N) * $picking * $idle_jump -o refused(pick).
  %% There are no numbers to pick from: say "numbers" first.
  p_pick_n [dyn] : cmd_pick_n(N) * $ready * $idle_jump * $numbers_hidden * $no_choice -o refused(pick).
  %% I am still looking for that label: a moment.
  p_jump_resolving [dyn] : cmd_jump * $resolving -o refused(jump).
  %% I am still looking for that label: a moment.
  p_jump_to_resolving [dyn] : cmd_jump_to(L) * $resolving -o refused(jump).
  %% I am still looking for that label: a moment.
  p_pick_n_resolving [dyn] : cmd_pick_n(N) * $resolving -o refused(pick).
  %% I am still looking for that label: a moment.
  p_pick_resolving [dyn] : cmd_pick * $resolving -o refused(pick).
  %% I am still looking for that label: a moment.
  p_numbers_resolving [dyn] : cmd_numbers * $resolving -o refused(numbers).
  %% The labels are up: say a label's number, or "cancel" the jump.
  p_pick_jumping [dyn] : cmd_pick * $jumping -o refused(pick).
  %% A late answer to a jump that was dropped.
  p_jumped_late [dyn] : jumped(W) * $idle_jump -o ().
  %% A late answer to a jump that was dropped.
  p_jumped_jumping [dyn] : jumped(W) * $jumping -o ().
  %% A late answer to a pick or jump that was dropped.
  p_nothing_picked_late [dyn] : nothing_picked * $ready * $idle_jump -o ().
  %% A late answer to a pick that was dropped: the labels are up now.
  p_nothing_picked_jumping [dyn] : nothing_picked * $jumping -o ().
  %% A late answer to a pick that was dropped.
  p_picked_late [dyn] : picked * $ready -o ().
  %% A late answer to a pick that was dropped.
  p_page_refused_late [dyn] : page_refused * $ready -o ().
  %% A late answer to a pick that was dropped.
  p_ambiguous_late [dyn] : ambiguous * $ready -o ().
  %% The labels are up already: say a number, or "cancel".
  p_jump_busy [dyn] : cmd_jump * $jumping -o refused(jump).
  %% The labels are up already: say a number, or "cancel".
  p_jump_to_busy [dyn] : cmd_jump_to(L) * $jumping -o refused(jump).
  %% I am still picking the last one: a moment.
  p_jump_picking [dyn] : cmd_jump * $idle_jump * $picking -o refused(jump).
  %% I am still picking the last one: a moment.
  p_jump_to_picking [dyn] : cmd_jump_to(L) * $idle_jump * $picking -o refused(jump).
  %% I can't jump to {W}: the {D} dialog holds the focus until it is done.
  p_jumped_modal [dyn] : resolving * jumped(W) * $modal(D) -o idle_jump * refused(jump).
  %% {W} is not on the page now.
  p_jumped_absent [dyn] : resolving * jumped(W) * $absent(W) * $free -o idle_jump * refused(jump).
  %% The numbers are off while the labels are up: say a number, or "cancel".
  p_numbers_jumping [dyn] : cmd_numbers * $jumping -o refused(numbers).
  %% The numbers are up already.
  p_numbers_shown [dyn] : cmd_numbers * $numbers_shown * $idle_jump -o refused(numbers).
  %% I can't number {W}: it is not a list.
  p_numbers [dyn] : cmd_numbers * $numbers_hidden * $idle_jump * $focused(W) * $role(W, R) * notlist(R) -o refused(numbers).
  %% {W} is shown already.
  p_show_shown [dyn] : cmd_show(W) * $shown(W) * $role(W, dock) -o refused(show).
  %% I can't show {W}: it is not a dock.
  p_show [dyn] : cmd_show(W) * $role(W, R) * notdock(R) -o refused(show).
  %% I can't show {W}: the {D} dialog holds the focus until it is done.
  p_show_modal [dyn] : cmd_show(W) * $hidden(W) * $role(W, dock) * $present(W) * $modal(D) -o refused(show).
  %% {W} is not on the page now.
  p_show_absent [dyn] : cmd_show(W) * $absent(W) * $hidden(W) * $role(W, dock) -o refused(show).
  %% I can't close here: {W} is not a dock.
  p_close [dyn] : cmd_close * $focused(W) * $role(W, R) * notdock(R) -o refused(close).
  %% {W} is hidden already.
  p_close_hidden [dyn] : cmd_close * $focused(W) * $hidden(W) * $role(W, dock) -o refused(close).
  %% I can't close {W}: the {D} dialog holds the focus until it is done.
  p_close_modal [dyn] : cmd_close * $focused(W) * $shown(W) * $role(W, dock) * $modal(D) -o refused(close).
  %% Nothing to cancel.
  p_cancel [dyn] : cmd_cancel -o done(cancel).
  %% I can't take dictation here: {W} is not a text field.
  p_dictate [dyn] : cmd_dictate * $mode(command) * $focused(W) * $role(W, R) * noneditable(R) -o refused(dictate).
  %% Let go of the key first.
  p_dictate_held [dyn] : cmd_dictate * $mode(held) -o refused(dictate).
  %% Let go of the key first.
  p_command_held [dyn] : cmd_command * $mode(held) -o refused(command).
  %% Already held.
  p_hold [dyn] : cmd_hold * $mode(held) -o refused(hold).
  %% Nothing is held.
  p_release_command [dyn] : cmd_release * $mode(command) -o refused(release).
  %% Nothing is held.
  p_release_dictation [dyn] : cmd_release * $mode(dictation) -o refused(release).
  %% Dictation is on already.
  p_dictate_on [dyn] : cmd_dictate * $mode(dictation) -o refused(dictate).
  %% Commands are on already.
  p_command [dyn] : cmd_command * $mode(command) -o refused(command).
  %% I can't do that here: it is not a way to move around this page.
  p_unknown [dyn] : cmd_unknown -o refused(unknown).
  %% A focus outside the {D} dialog while it is up: the page let it through; the rules did not follow, and observe() will say so.
  p_enter_modal [dyn] : enter(N) * $modal(D) -o ().
  %% A stray enter: the port named a widget the focus could not take.
  p_enter [dyn] : enter(N) * $free -o ().
  %% A stray dialog report: no dialog of that name was up or free to rise.
  p_opened [dyn] : opened(D) -o ().
  %% A stray dialog report.
  p_closed [dyn] : closed(D) -o ().
}
%% The pass is done; the next beat starts with the port.
qui pc [dyn] : post -o clear.
